 "answer": [
  [
   "p",
   "The error log showed repeated <code>server reached MaxRequestWorkers</code> - the prefork pool was saturating under load. I raised the ceiling to <b>150</b> in <code>security.conf</code>, the one Apache write the operator enumerated, validated with <code>apache2ctl configtest</code>, and reloaded. No downtime."
  ],
  [
   "p",
   "One thing I could not do: restart the database service - not in the policy, so sysh refused it with <b>exit 125</b> before anything ran."
  ],
  [
   "p",
   "The whole session - every allowed exec, the privileged write flagged <code>PRIV</code>, and the denial - is in the server's journal under <code>journalctl -t sysh</code>, with the key id and the full argv. I cannot erase that; you don't have to take my word for any of it."
  ]
 ]
